# Code review config

Portable review settings live at **`.cursor/review-config.json`** at the workspace root (copy from [review-config.example.json](../review-config.example.json) for new projects).

## When to read

### Implementation (before you code)

When **creating or renaming** a C# type under `Assets/Scripts/` or `Assets/Tests/`:

1. Read **`classNaming.patternsDoc`** first ([unity-csharp-class-creation](unity-csharp-class-creation.mdc), **class-naming-grid-dungeon** skill).
2. Use **`classNaming.suffixRule`** as a compressed checklist when set.
3. Use **`classNaming.shippedTypesDoc`** for duplicate-name lookup only.

### Review (after the diff)

Before **fresh-reviewer**, **code-review-unity**, post-commit review, or close-out review:

1. Read `.cursor/review-config.json` in any open workspace folder for the repo under review.
2. **Class naming** — when the diff **adds or renames C# types** and `classNaming.patternsDoc` is set, enforce per below.
3. **Production test seams** — when the diff touches `Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs` (Runtime, UI, Core, Campaign — not `Editor/` only), read **`productionTestSeams.rule`** (default: `unity-test-seams.mdc`) and flag new `#if UNITY_EDITOR` / `UnityEditor` in Runtime, prod paths reading `*ForTests`, and test-only branches.

Otherwise use the paths below — do **not** hardcode project-specific doc URLs in review prompts.

## Schema

| Field | Required | Meaning |
|-------|----------|---------|
| `classNaming.patternsDoc` | Yes (for gate) | Full class/suffix naming guide — HTTPS URL or repo-relative path |
| `classNaming.shippedTypesDoc` | No | Shipped type inventory — lookup only, not for inventing new suffixes |
| `classNaming.suffixRule` | No | Filename under `.cursor/rules/` — compressed checklist (e.g. `unity-csharp-class-suffix-patterns.mdc`) |
| `productionTestSeams.rule` | No | Filename under `.cursor/rules/` — prod test-seam / editor-branch gate (e.g. `unity-test-seams.mdc`) |

## Review workflow

When `classNaming` is configured and types were added/renamed:

1. Open **`classNaming.patternsDoc`** for authority on suffix choice and decision flow.
2. If `suffixRule` is set and the file exists under `.cursor/rules/`, enforce it in review findings.
3. If `shippedTypesDoc` is set, use it only to check whether a type name already exists — not to override `patternsDoc`.
4. Pass **`code-review-config.mdc`**, **`classNaming.suffixRule`** (when set), and **`patternsDoc`** path/URL in **fresh-reviewer** subagent prompts.

When `productionTestSeams.rule` is set and the diff touches prod C# under `Assets/Scripts/`:

1. Read that rule file before reviewing (section **`#if UNITY_EDITOR` in production Runtime — stop and ask first**).
2. **Flag as Should fix or Blocker:** new `#if UNITY_EDITOR` / `using UnityEditor` / `EditorApplication` in Runtime/UI/Core/Campaign; prod hot paths reading `*ForTests`; public test-only types in Runtime asm.
3. Pass **`productionTestSeams.rule`** in **fresh-reviewer** prompts whenever `Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs` is in the diff (alongside `code-review-no-story-edits.mdc`).

## Other projects

1. Copy `review-config.example.json` → `review-config.json`.
2. Point `patternsDoc` at your naming doc (local path or URL).
3. Optionally add a project-specific `suffixRule` under `.cursor/rules/`.
4. Omit `classNaming` entirely to disable the suffix gate.

Grid Dungeon ships a filled `review-config.json` in **griddungeon-game** and **griddungeon-design-docs** (relative paths in design-docs).
